CHAPTER 88.1	(a)	The transfer and increment occur concurrently, i.e., at the same clock edge. After the transfer, R holds the contents that were in R1 before the clock edge, and R2 holds its previous value incremented by 1.				Verilog				R2 <= R1 + 1;				R1 <= R				VHDL				R2 <= R1+ ''1';				R1 <= R;(b)	Decrement the content of R3 by one.				Verilog				R3 <= R3 - 1;								VHDL				R3 <= R3 - '1';(c)	If (S1 = 1), transfer content of R1 to R0; otherwise, if (S1 = 0 and S2 = 1), transfer content of R2 to R0.				Verilog				if (S1 == 1) the R0 <= R1; else if (S1 == 0 && S2 == 1) then R0 <= R2;				VHDL				if S1 = 1 then R0 <= R1; elsif S1 = 0 and S2 = 1 then R0 <= R2;	 8.2
